Z||000000||bHooper||05-12-2000||09:22 AM||||I had been looking at the next major project on my GT... the suspension.  I was considering some of the serious mods out there, such as the Shelby Custom exotics coil over conversion kits for the front and rear, as well as Ryans motorsports bump steer kit for the rear.<P>However, last night, while we were working on my buddy's seized caliper, his brother shows up.  His brother does a <B>LOT</B> of SCCA racing, in his Mercedes 190e 2.?L 24v "rocketship", when I explained some of the things that I was interested in (and their cost) he went into shock!<P>Apparently, he knows a local guy that used to build IMSA cars, and now builds race suspensions, ect, for people.  This guy redid all 4 corners of his friends BMW for $600!!!... giving him adjustable camber, tow in and ride hight.  And he feels confident that he can do something similar for me!  I will just have to leave the car with the guy for about 3 weeks or so.  Heck if it gets cheaper, he can have it for 2 months!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Needless to say, I am very interested to see what this guy has to offer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I'm all for saving money and improveing performance!<P>We also had a little discusion about exhaust systems, I will tell you about that later.<P>hoop||||reg||6
